@lordchosen19  People do MBA abroad after MBAs in India because MBAs in India count as MiMs abroad lol. People from IIM ABCL go abroad and do another MBA from Kellogg. You are exactly the kind of person who selects himself out of the application pool bc you're too dumb to compete.

IIMs have zero value abroad. No indian MBA has much value. Only IITs in engineering have respect. No one abroad knows what an "IIM" is. ISB ranks higher than ABC in FT Rankings which is all someone abroad would care to look at. You're basing your opinion off of an ISB alum choosing to do a second MBA which literally dozens of IIM grads do a year? Which of these did you get an offer from? Have you converted ABC, ISB or XLRI? I personally know of people who have left IIM L and XLRI for ISB. Only ABC is better than ISB.

The fact you say "IIM" is better than ISB tells me all I need to know about your validity. There are 21 IIMs in the country and barely 7 of 8 of them are good. The rest barely quality for tier 2 colleges. Whenever someone mentions "IIM" to gauge a college's level when it's an umbrella term for 21 vastly differing institutions is when you know he's one of the angoor khatte crowd.

